{"format":1,"seq":123,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I realize args aren't retained at runtime, so I'd need to infer function calls statically from source via regex since traces alone won't have them -- but destructured calls like `run(\"check\")` from `npm: { run }` wouldn't match a simple `x.y(` pattern, so I need a different detection approach.\n\nInstead, I'm considering parsing npm's own banner output since it prints the script name as it runs -- something like matching lines starting with `>` that show the package and script name, accounting for scoped package names too.\n\nThis feels self-contained and testable, but I should consider edge cases like workspaces printing a path suffix, truncated stdout dropping the banner, or `loglevel=silent` suppressing it entirely, each needing a sensible fallback like \"run, exit 0\".\n\nActually, maybe the renderer already has access to a command field through ProcessResult or DisplayProcessResult, so I should check those fields before building a custom parser.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_016CC4qH3PcYM8JpcWRoFK35","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Inspect process result parsing and npm command runner\"}\nasync ({ workspace: { search, read } }) => {\n  const [p, n] = await Promise.all([\n    search(\"export (interface|type) DisplayProcessResult|export function parseProcessResult\", { regex: true, path: \"src/process\", contextLines: 10 }),\n    read(\"src/functions/commands/npm.ts\", { format: \"raw\" }),\n  ]);\n  return { p: p.matches.map(m => `${m.file}:${m.line}\\n${m.text}\\n${m.after.map(a=>a.text).join(\"\\n\")}`), n: n.content.slice(0, 3000) };\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"nvidia","model":"aws/anthropic/bedrock-claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":1237,"cacheRead":46528,"cacheWrite":431,"totalTokens":48198,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"ca